## Final Project Summary

AI Interview Coach is a fully deployed, tested, production-hardened AI web application: real LLM-generated interview questions (optionally personalized), detailed 8-dimension AI feedback per answer, persistent session history, and an analytics dashboard — built entirely on free-tier tools, with 28 passing automated tests and a documented, defensible architecture.

## Lessons Learned

- **An abstraction is only proven once it survives a real change under pressure** — the `AIProvider` interface was a good idea on Day 2; it became a *proven* good idea on Day 5.
- **"Code-complete" and "verified working" are different claims, and conflating them costs more time later** — the Day 6/7 deployment saga was long specifically because early attempts didn't distinguish between the two.
- **The first error message is often not the real one** — true on Day 3 (pandas), and true again, more expensively, on Day 7 (six layers deep).
- **Free-tier constraints are a legitimate design input, not just a budget footnote** — they directly shaped two of this project's most important decisions (Days 3 and 5).

